#
# Commit message template (TRAINING.md, rule 3). Lines starting with # are
# dropped from the message.
#
# Subject: what this commit does, in the imperative, at most 72 characters.
#
# Why: what was wrong or missing, and how you decided on this fix.
#
# Checked: what you ran or looked at, and what it returned. For example:
#   "Checked: rm -rf _build && bazel run //:docs is green, warnings.txt is empty;
#    the rendered release note shows the list as a list."
#
# "Closes #<n>" belongs in the pull request description, not here.
